    "q-161038": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161038",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14131711/assets/aa5b04b98d3796656fca912d8dc1732ea7e12bab9083f8ca543ad5fd4fdb10ff.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the quarter-circle shown above. What is ${∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $4$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-161038-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"49\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-msubsup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222B TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.896em; margin-left: -0.388em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\" style=\"margin-left: 0.647em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2F\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 1.503em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-msubsup space=\"2\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222B TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.896em; margin-left: -0.388em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\" style=\"margin-left: 0.647em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 1.513em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-msup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D452 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.413em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.222em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx