    "q-161070": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161070",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "If $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 16,\\,y\\le 0\\},$ then ${∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A=$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14131711/assets/d882bf70ecb7b94eee0eeeffbf63874ca8607268167f96278deb4678ec3b827a.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $4$ centered at $(4,0).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=16$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4)}^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +16+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =16 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14131711/assets/605d9ce1c9030d1ac83c0a320bd648b42893f222279dd2d56b111acd9957c202.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (the negative $y$-axis) and $\\theta =0$ (the positive $x$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14131711/assets/f37e34042338af2b1ba5f0c214ebf046eeba068b0b3238b662910a868c069ee4.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r{e}^{{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r{e}^{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r{e}^{{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-161070-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"105\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-msubsup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222B TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.896em; margin-left: -0.388em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\" style=\"margin-left: 0.647em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 1.446em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2F\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-msubsup space=\"2\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222B TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.896em; margin-left: -0.388em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\" style=\"margin-left: 0.647em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c63\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6F\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"2\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D703 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-texatom><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 1.498em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-msup space=\"2\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D452 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.413em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-msup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c64\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c64\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D703 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><msubsup><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∫</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo>/</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∫</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>8</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mtext>d</mtext><mi>r</mi><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mtext>d</mtext><mi>θ</mi></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> "
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-161070-b",
